---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '@/lib/urls';
---
<Layout title="How We Use AI" description="Mindlab’s standards for AI in strategy, content, and campaigns.">
  <section class="page-hero container">
    <h1>How We Use AI</h1>
    <p class="lede">AI can help us explore ideas and draft options. A person at Mindlab is responsible for the final work.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-compact">
    <div class="container reading-width privacy-copy">
      <h2>Where AI can help</h2>
      <p>We may use AI to brainstorm angles, organize approved research, outline content, and draft copy variations. At kickoff, we record any limits the client sets for their project and follow them throughout the engagement.</p>

      <h2>People review the work</h2>
      <p>A Mindlab team member reviews client-facing work before it goes out. We verify material claims, quotes, and numbers against the underlying sources, check for bias and misleading wording, and confirm that assets are appropriate for the intended use. We ask for evidence or revise the work when a claim lacks support.</p>

      <h2>Client information stays protected</h2>
      <p>We use tools approved for the project and share only the information needed for the task. We keep credentials out of AI tools. Confidential material or personal data requires explicit client authorization and a tool approved for that data. We remove identifying details where possible.</p>

      <h2>We disclose AI use when it matters</h2>
      <p>We agree disclosure expectations with the client and identify generated imagery, audio, or video when a viewer could mistake it for a real person, place, event, or result. We also follow applicable client and platform disclosure requirements. We exclude invented testimonials and results from client work. In our portfolio, we label fictional companies, mock assets, and illustrative figures as concept work.</p>

      <h2>Questions or corrections</h2>
      <p><a href={withBase('/book-call/')}>Contact Mindlab</a> to ask how we use AI on a project, request limits, or flag something we should review.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
